// A store the control flow can SKIP must refuse on the general path.
//
// The flatten runs every block unconditionally, so a store the original
// program could jump past commits a value the branch was there to
// suppress.  CF-1a refused every store outside the exit block; the rule
// is now the reachability question that is actually being asked -
// removing the store's block must disconnect the exit from the entry -
// which lets a store the flow CANNOT skip through, and this fixture is
// the other side of that line.
//
// Nothing rescues this one: `o` is stored only on the true arm, the false
// arm reaches the exit without it and without a discard, so a fragment
// that took the false arm would be painted with the true arm's value.
// The refusal has to be seen to fire, or the relaxation next to it is a
// claim rather than a bound.
void main(float4 c : TEXCOORD0, float4 d : TEXCOORD1, out float4 o : COLOR)
{
    if (c.a < 0.5) {
        o = c * 2.0;
    }
}
